    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Diamond Hoo Ha is the sixth and final studio album by Supergrass, released in 2008 on Parlophone. It finds the band turning away from the more reflective tone of Road to Rouen and back toward a punchier, riff-driven sound, with a brisk mix of garage rock energy, Britpop melody, and slyly playful lyrics.\n\nProduced by Nick Launay, the album was widely heard as a return to form, even if it did not radically reinvent the group’s formula. Its opening pair of singles, “Diamond Hoo Ha Man” and “Bad Blood,” set the tone with sharp hooks and a harder-edged attack, while tracks like “Rough Knuckles” and “Rebel In You” reinforced the record’s lean, energetic character. It reached No. 19 in the UK, making it Supergrass’s lowest-charting studio album, but it remains a strong late-period statement from a band that had always balanced wit, swagger, and melodic instinct.",
